<problem><title>Video review questions</title>
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />

<p>Which of the following statements about the Forward Euler algorithm for solving autonomous differential equations is <alert>incorrect</alert>?</p>
  <answer name="ans1">
    <choice>it provides a way to approximate the behavior of solutions to the differential equation based on tangent line approximations computed at discrete time steps</choice>
    <choice>its a useful way to glean information about the behavior of solutions when you know the function <m>f(x)</m> but you don't have an analytic solution (i.e. an equation for <m>x(t)</m>) for the differential equation</choice>
    <choice credit="1">it's a technique for determining information about solutions solely based on the graph of the differential equation </choice>
    <choice>the approximation improves with smaller time steps since the slopes of unique solutions are likely changing continuously over time</choice>
  </answer>
</exercise>
</problem>
</section>


